63
00:04:33,980 --> 00:04:38,980
And so we took to the stage at EFS.

64
00:04:41,260 --> 00:04:46,280
Sadly we sold 500 tickets in a 30,000 seat stadium.

65
00:04:46,280 --> 00:04:55,200
That's like barely over 1%, which means we stopped going up and just bombed.

66
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:57,420
It would have been weird to do an encore after that.

67
00:04:57,420 --> 00:04:58,860
So we put the new song on the shelf.

68
00:04:58,860 --> 00:05:01,800
Plus the unsolved tickets put us in debt big time.

69
00:05:01,800 --> 00:05:04,600
It stunk, even for zombies!

70
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:07,100
Could this be the end?

71
00:05:13,100 --> 00:05:15,600
The EFS show was a huge disaster.

72
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:18,200
But we still want to get on stage together again.

73
00:05:18,200 --> 00:05:20,300
That's why we each picked up part-time jobs

74
00:05:20,300 --> 00:05:22,400
to try and bring ourselves out of the red.

75
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:24,900
We're not going to give up.

76
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:26,600
Oh, yeah.

77
00:05:26,600 --> 00:05:30,700
And as for our fearless producer, Mr. Kotaro...

78
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:33,100
What's that?

79
00:05:33,100 --> 00:05:34,600
Pope's nose?

80
00:05:34,600 --> 00:05:36,600
Why's it called that?

81
00:05:36,600 --> 00:05:39,600
Oh, you want me to save Saga, Your Holiness?

82
00:05:41,600 --> 00:05:43,100
Sorry, it ain't happening!

83
00:05:43,100 --> 00:05:45,100
This is the Saga-pocalypse!

84
00:05:45,100 --> 00:05:46,600
No, it's Saga, get it!

85
00:05:49,100 --> 00:05:50,600
I knew that.

86
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:52,600
Which is why I was hoping that I could.

87
00:05:53,600 --> 00:05:55,600
This stuff's named after a nose!

88
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:56,800
Pope's nose!

89
00:05:56,800 --> 00:05:58,600
Man, that's gotta feel bad!

90
00:06:00,600 --> 00:06:01,600
Morning, sir!

91
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:04,100
I'm Saga's new milk delivery girl!

92
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:08,600
Don't move!

93
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:09,800
This stuff is tricky.

94
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,300
I can never seem to master the blend.

95
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:17,600
It just doesn't look, I don't know, lively enough?

96
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:19,600
Well, we are dead.

97
00:06:20,100 --> 00:06:21,000
I knew it.

98
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:22,400
The color is still off.

99
00:06:22,400 --> 00:06:24,100
I sure wish Kotaro was here.

100
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:26,600
What the hell's the matter with that guy?

101
00:06:26,600 --> 00:06:29,400
I'll go check on him one more time.

102
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:33,400
Excuse me!

103
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:34,600
Is he here?

104
00:06:40,600 --> 00:06:41,900
It's me, sir.

105
00:06:41,900 --> 00:06:42,900
Sakura.

106
00:06:43,900 --> 00:06:44,900
Are you okay?

107
00:06:44,900 --> 00:06:48,700
Oh no, why is it so dark?

108
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:50,700
Because you're way overdue for a haircut.

109
00:06:50,700 --> 00:06:53,500
Oh great, it's you again.

110
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:55,500
I don't think this is good for your health.

111
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:58,500
Hey, guess what?

112
00:06:58,500 --> 00:07:00,000
We worked really hard this month,

113
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:01,500
and we brought in some extra money.

114
00:07:05,500 --> 00:07:06,500
Listen, sir.

115
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:11,300
Yes, that show is practically a second death sentence for us.

116
00:07:11,300 --> 00:07:14,300
But we rose from the dead once,

117
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:16,300
and I know that we can do it again.

118
00:07:16,300 --> 00:07:18,800
And when we do, we'll be even stronger.

119
00:07:18,800 --> 00:07:20,300
It's over, and that's that.

120
00:07:20,300 --> 00:07:21,300
No, it isn't.

121
00:07:21,300 --> 00:07:23,300
Now I'm not sure when exactly,

122
00:07:23,300 --> 00:07:25,300
but we will pay off that debt.

123
00:07:25,300 --> 00:07:27,300
No matter how long it might take us,

124
00:07:27,300 --> 00:07:29,300
we'll keep on giving it all we've got.

125
00:07:29,300 --> 00:07:33,100
I'm done.

126
00:07:33,100 --> 00:07:34,100
Just go.

127
00:07:34,100 --> 00:07:36,100
But sir,

128
00:07:36,100 --> 00:07:38,100
we're supposed to be performing at Guile soon,

129
00:07:38,100 --> 00:07:40,100
the metal spot where we debuted.

130
00:07:40,100 --> 00:07:42,100
We thought if we went back there,

131
00:07:42,100 --> 00:07:44,600
maybe Fran Shushu could get a fresh start.

132
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:48,100
We never sang that last song you wrote us,

133
00:07:48,100 --> 00:07:50,100
so we're gonna do it on that stage.

134
00:07:50,100 --> 00:07:53,100
And I want you to be there, Mr. Kotaro.

135
00:07:59,300 --> 00:08:05,100
Hey, what's the problem?

136
00:08:05,100 --> 00:08:06,100
You nerd.

137
00:08:06,100 --> 00:08:08,100
You're all scrunched up like a pope's nose.

138
00:08:08,100 --> 00:08:09,100
Look at yourself.

139
00:08:09,100 --> 00:08:12,100
Hey, Sakuna, say I'm a chicken butt.

140
00:08:12,100 --> 00:08:13,100
Come on, do it.

141
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:15,100
It'll be funny.

142
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:18,100
I wish I knew how to get him back to his old self again.

143
00:08:18,100 --> 00:08:22,100
Yeah, it sounds like he's been on a bender for a solid month now.

144
00:08:22,100 --> 00:08:24,100
He may be a little out there,

145
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:26,100
but I think it'll be hard to operate without him,

146
00:08:26,100 --> 00:08:28,100
if not impossible.

147
00:08:28,100 --> 00:08:30,900
Hey, girls, I'm just spitballing here.

148
00:08:30,900 --> 00:08:33,900
But what if this isn't about the money?

149
00:08:33,900 --> 00:08:37,900
And perhaps there's something he's been hiding from all of us.

150
00:08:37,900 --> 00:08:38,900
I mean, think about it.

151
00:08:38,900 --> 00:08:42,900
Why did he choose that time for us to perform at EFS?

152
00:08:42,900 --> 00:08:43,900
Good point.

153
00:08:43,900 --> 00:08:45,900
He couldn't have thought the event would sell out.

154
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:48,900
So, like, he was in a rush maybe?

155
00:08:48,900 --> 00:08:49,900
Why though?

156
00:08:49,900 --> 00:08:50,900
I don't know.

157
00:08:50,900 --> 00:08:53,900
Well then, if Lady Ai is correct,

158
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:55,900
I think we should try to assist him.

159
00:08:55,900 --> 00:08:57,900
Though we need to discern what the trouble is.

160
00:08:57,900 --> 00:09:01,700
I bet we could figure it out if we went snooping around his office.

161
00:09:08,700 --> 00:09:09,700
It's open.

162
00:09:09,700 --> 00:09:11,700
Hell yeah!

163
00:09:11,700 --> 00:09:13,500
Let's clean him out!

164
00:09:13,500 --> 00:09:14,500
Yay!

165
00:09:14,500 --> 00:09:15,500
Guys, be careful!

166
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:16,500
Whoa!

167
00:09:16,500 --> 00:09:17,500
Check out all this junk!

168
00:09:26,500 --> 00:09:28,500
Remember not to break anything, okay?

169
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:33,300
Ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow, ow!

170
00:09:35,300 --> 00:09:37,300
Crap, I'm in trouble!

171
00:09:37,300 --> 00:09:52,560
This is the encore we never got to sing.

172
00:09:52,560 --> 00:09:55,020
It must be a rough draft, huh?

173
00:09:55,020 --> 00:09:55,780
No!

174
00:09:55,780 --> 00:09:57,260
Okay, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

175
00:09:57,260 --> 00:09:58,540
Oh, yeah!

176
00:09:58,540 --> 00:10:02,160
La, la, la, la, la, la, la.

177
00:10:02,160 --> 00:10:05,620
I guess this is what his songwriting process is like.

178
00:10:05,620 --> 00:10:08,740
You can tell that he really cares.

179
00:10:08,740 --> 00:10:11,780
Or used to, at least.

180
00:10:11,780 --> 00:10:16,620
We still haven't figured out why he was in such a hurry for us to go big.

181
00:10:16,620 --> 00:10:20,540
Yeah, but now we know how he felt about the EFS show.

182
00:10:20,540 --> 00:10:24,540
Next time we sing, we have to make sure Mr. Kotaro's there.

183
00:10:24,540 --> 00:10:27,540
If we can finally perform that encore song on stage,

184
00:10:27,540 --> 00:10:30,420
then maybe he'll go back to his old self again.

185
00:10:30,420 --> 00:10:33,260
Once he feels better, he'll explain everything.

186
00:10:33,260 --> 00:10:36,380
I'm not sure it'll work, but we should definitely try.

187
00:10:36,380 --> 00:10:40,380
Yeah, and at the next show, that song will knock him right on his ass!

188
00:10:40,380 --> 00:10:41,380
Right!

189
00:10:41,380 --> 00:10:42,500
Ha, ha, ha!

190
00:10:42,500 --> 00:10:43,500
Ha, ha!

191
00:10:43,500 --> 00:10:47,500
Ha, ha, ha!

192
00:10:47,500 --> 00:11:03,500
Ha, ha, ha!

193
00:11:03,500 --> 00:11:15,960
Here you are, m'lord.

194
00:11:16,720 --> 00:11:20,460
Reporting in after another grueling day of defending justice in Saga.

195
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:26,220
I swear, babe, the drinks you pour me at the end of these long shifts are always so sweet.

196
00:11:26,380 --> 00:11:29,620
My pleasure. Thank you for taking such good care of Saga.

197
00:11:29,940 --> 00:11:30,500
Grape, sir.

198
00:11:30,500 --> 00:11:32,380
Uh, just doing my job.

199
00:11:32,620 --> 00:11:33,100
Gorgeous.

200
00:11:33,500 --> 00:11:35,400
I'll keep coming to see you every night.

201
00:11:36,100 --> 00:11:37,760
Your eyes are so arresting.

202
00:11:39,360 --> 00:11:41,640
Kay, I'm here. Where's the party?

203
00:11:46,140 --> 00:11:46,980
My bad.

204
00:11:46,980 --> 00:12:05,800
Lord Kotorou, methinks you've had too much to drink.

205
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:06,940
What?

206
00:12:06,940 --> 00:12:21,100
I was wrong. I was wrong. I was wrong. I was wrong. So, so wrong. Wrong.

207
00:12:21,100 --> 00:12:37,620
Okay. If we can do that on stage, we're set. Oh, trust me, we're gonna kill it. But, Mr. Kotorou, I guess we never heard anything from the boozer.

208
00:12:37,620 --> 00:12:44,620
After what Yugiri saw last night, it isn't surprising. The poor man was practically coming apart at the seams.

209
00:12:44,620 --> 00:12:50,960
Please don't worry, you guys. Just stay focused on getting ready for the set. I'll go and get him.

210
00:12:50,960 --> 00:12:59,820
The show is tonight. Will you please listen to me?

211
00:12:59,820 --> 00:13:02,560
I told you, do whatever you want.

212
00:13:02,760 --> 00:13:07,800
I'm just asking you to show up. The girls and I love your songs. We want to keep performing them.

213
00:13:07,800 --> 00:13:11,900
I know some bad stuff happened, but that's not a reason for us to quit being idols.

214
00:13:14,460 --> 00:13:17,400
Look, there's nothing more I can do for you.

215
00:13:21,180 --> 00:13:26,240
What happened, Mr. Kotorou? Don't you remember what you said to me back then?

216
00:13:27,240 --> 00:13:31,680
I have what it takes! I'll never, never abandon you!

217
00:13:32,380 --> 00:13:35,060
Where's the old you? Because we need him right now.

218
00:13:35,060 --> 00:13:38,720
He didn't have what it takes.

219
00:13:40,220 --> 00:13:43,540
Whatever! I'm done trying! Forget you!

220
00:13:57,920 --> 00:14:03,280
You guys, we have to make sure this concert is a success, even without a producer.

221
00:14:05,060 --> 00:14:13,660
Yeah, we haven't been here lately. Looks like they've got a totally new crowd.

222
00:14:14,180 --> 00:14:16,260
I'm sure how Fashushi will be all right.

223
00:14:17,280 --> 00:14:19,100
Bit of a rally lot to play after EFS.

224
00:14:19,880 --> 00:14:22,820
Yeah, and that makes this a really important night for them.

225
00:14:23,100 --> 00:14:24,900
All the more reason to show our support.

226
00:14:25,440 --> 00:14:25,880
Indeed!

227
00:14:25,880 --> 00:14:33,840
What? Idols? What the hell?

228
00:14:34,480 --> 00:14:34,880
Fashushi!

229
00:14:35,580 --> 00:14:36,880
Look off, socks off!

230
00:14:39,380 --> 00:14:41,080
Stop wasting our time!

231
00:14:41,180 --> 00:14:42,260
Yeah, get on with it.

232
00:14:42,300 --> 00:14:43,340
This is lame.

233
00:14:43,340 --> 00:14:46,500
Uh, hey guys! We're Fraud Shoo Shoo!

234
00:14:46,600 --> 00:14:47,120
That's them.

235
00:14:47,180 --> 00:14:52,840
See, a little while ago we did a show at EFS that went kind of haywire and we can't let it end like that.

236
00:14:52,900 --> 00:14:57,140
So we're trying to make a comeback starting tonight, right here, right now, okay?

237
00:14:57,580 --> 00:15:01,060
So, uh, thanks for coming to the first stop on our little revenge tour.

238
00:15:01,500 --> 00:15:02,480
You ready to rock?

239
00:15:02,480 --> 00:15:14,640
It's not a big crowd, and it's nothing we haven't done before.

240
00:15:15,220 --> 00:15:17,120
Let's put EFS behind us.

241
00:15:20,640 --> 00:15:21,660
It's okay.

242
00:15:22,540 --> 00:15:23,520
It's okay.

243
00:15:23,520 --> 00:15:33,600
How long do you plan to darken my bar with that pathetic look?

244
00:15:34,420 --> 00:15:37,140
Is the verbal abuse included in the bill?

245
00:15:37,280 --> 00:15:41,400
Most of my customers don't sleep here overnight because they're afraid to go home.

246
00:15:42,920 --> 00:15:45,120
Look, you said that you're done, right?

247
00:15:45,600 --> 00:15:48,460
What was it called again? The Zombie World Super Project?

248
00:15:48,780 --> 00:15:50,680
The Zombieland Saga Project.

249
00:15:51,340 --> 00:15:52,160
Yeah, that.

250
00:15:52,160 --> 00:15:55,300
It was a crazy idea in the first place.

251
00:15:55,700 --> 00:15:57,940
A bunch of undead turned pop stars?

252
00:15:58,980 --> 00:16:01,240
Your Sagaettes will get over it, too.

253
00:16:01,560 --> 00:16:05,240
It'll be a nice memory for them while they wander the earth for eternity.

254
00:16:05,820 --> 00:16:07,740
Their name is Fraun Shoo Shoo.

255
00:16:08,120 --> 00:16:11,440
Zombies don't sing and dance. Let them get on with their lives.

256
00:16:11,820 --> 00:16:14,060
I mean, they're dead, but you know what I'm saying.

257
00:16:14,120 --> 00:16:15,900
This project has a crucial deadline!

258
00:16:17,940 --> 00:16:21,880
After they died on stage, worse than any living idol group ever did,

259
00:16:21,880 --> 00:16:26,660
and then got stuck with a massive debt! There's no way it'll work now! Even you know that!

260
00:16:26,660 --> 00:16:28,800
All right, fine.

261
00:16:29,800 --> 00:16:35,560
You demanded the impossible out of those girls from day one, and they still found a way to make it happen.

262
00:16:35,560 --> 00:16:40,040
So, if this latest hurdle is something you don't believe they can overcome,

263
00:16:40,540 --> 00:16:42,220
well, then you're probably right.

264
00:16:43,080 --> 00:16:48,440
